            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am afraid, this is a known limitation of \"tag\" surrounding. It uses Lua pattern matches by default so making it work robustly in all cases of hierarchical structure (like nested tags) is nearly impossible. The recommendation is to use tree-sitter surrounding if user wants a more robust behavior.\n\nA duplicate of (at least) #755.",
